            {
               "text": "### Prerequisites\n\nTo get the most out of this lesson, we recommend reading these texts first:\n\n- **Gravity as a Central Force**: why gravity is a central force that pulls objects toward the center of a planet, instead of pushing them \"down\" (<htcite0>)\n- **Walking on the Circle**: how the sine and cosine functions change as we walk around a circle (<htcite1>)\n- **Are we tangent to the planet?**: how a line that just touches a round planet helps us understand the tangent of an angle (<htcite2>)\n- **Where are we on a disk?**: how to locate a point on a flat disk using two coordinates, <b>r</b> × cos(<b>θ</b>) and <b>r</b> × sin(<b>θ</b>) (<htcite3>)",
