            {
               "text": "<p><h3>Where are we on a sphere?</h3>In the previous section, we extracted a flat disc from a sphere and learned to position ourselves on it. Now, let’s try a practical exercise:</p><p><center><div class=\"first_steps_lab_parent\"><div class=\"first_steps_lab question_mark\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-microscope\"></i></div><div class=\"first_steps_lab\"><b>Creating a Sphere</b><br /><br />Draw a circle on a sheet of paper; you can use a plate as a guide, tracing around it with a pencil. Then, cut out the circle. Place it in front of you horizontally, and spin it a few times toward your feet.</div></div></center></p>",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p class=\"desc\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 800 620\" role=\"img\" preserveAspectRatio=\"xMidYMid meet\" style=\"width:100%; height:auto; max-width:760px; display:block; margin:0 auto;\" aria-label=\"Four drawings showing the steps of the Creating a Sphere practice: draw a circle around a plate, cut it out, place it flat and spin it\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"10\" width=\"380\" height=\"290\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#fbfbf7\" stroke=\"#d9d9d2\"/><rect x=\"410\" y=\"10\" width=\"380\" height=\"290\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#fbfbf7\" stroke=\"#d9d9d2\"/><rect x=\"10\" y=\"320\" width=\"380\" height=\"290\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#fbfbf7\" stroke=\"#d9d9d2\"/><rect x=\"410\" y=\"320\" width=\"380\" height=\"290\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#fbfbf7\" stroke=\"#d9d9d2\"/><circle cx=\"42\" cy=\"46\" r=\"18\" fill=\"#2f6fb3\"/><text x=\"42\" y=\"53\" font-size=\"20\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-weight=\"bold\">1</text><circle cx=\"442\" cy=\"46\" r=\"18\" fill=\"#2f6fb3\"/><text x=\"442\" y=\"53\" font-size=\"20\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-weight=\"bold\">2</text><circle cx=\"42\" cy=\"356\" r=\"18\" fill=\"#2f6fb3\"/><text x=\"42\" y=\"363\" font-size=\"20\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-weight=\"bold\">3</text><circle cx=\"442\" cy=\"356\" r=\"18\" fill=\"#2f6fb3\"/><text x=\"442\" y=\"363\" font-size=\"20\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-weight=\"bold\">4</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"85\" width=\"240\" height=\"150\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#fffdf5\" stroke=\"#cfc9b8\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"160\" r=\"55\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#8a8a8a\" stroke-width=\"4\"/><g transform=\"translate(292,80) rotate(35)\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"10\" height=\"60\" fill=\"#f1c40f\" stroke=\"#b7950b\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><polygon points=\"0,60 10,60 5,74\" fill=\"#d35400\"/></g><circle cx=\"600\" cy=\"160\" r=\"55\" fill=\"#fff7d6\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"4\"/><line x1=\"690\" y1=\"102\" x2=\"720\" y2=\"72\" stroke=\"#7f8c8d\" stroke-width=\"6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"690\" y1=\"72\" x2=\"720\" y2=\"102\" stroke=\"#7f8c8d\" stroke-width=\"6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><circle cx=\"683\" cy=\"108\" r=\"7\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#7f8c8d\" stroke-width=\"4\"/><circle cx=\"683\" cy=\"66\" r=\"7\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#7f8c8d\" stroke-width=\"4\"/><ellipse cx=\"200\" cy=\"430\" rx=\"105\" ry=\"32\" fill=\"#fff7d6\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"4\"/><line x1=\"75\" y1=\"480\" x2=\"325\" y2=\"480\" stroke=\"#cfc9b8\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><ellipse cx=\"600\" cy=\"440\" rx=\"100\" ry=\"30\" fill=\"#fff7d6\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"4\"/><path d=\"M 520,420 C 535,365 665,365 680,420\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#c0392b\" stroke-width=\"5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><polygon points=\"670,412 684,422 671,430\" fill=\"#c0392b\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"280\" font-size=\"22\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#222222\" font-weight=\"bold\">Draw a circle</text><text x=\"600\" y=\"280\" font-size=\"22\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#222222\" font-weight=\"bold\">Cut it out</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"580\" font-size=\"22\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#222222\" font-weight=\"bold\">Place it flat</text><text x=\"600\" y=\"580\" font-size=\"22\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#222222\" font-weight=\"bold\">Spin it</text></svg></p><p class=\"desc\"><b>Figure 2</b>: The steps of the \"Creating a Sphere\" practice: draw a circle around a plate, cut it out, place it flat and spin it toward your feet.</p>",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "By spinning the circle, we representing a sphere, similar to our planet, as shown in the image in this section. This exercise also highlights the need to define an additional variable to locate ourselves beyond a flat disc. This extra variable, represented by the Greek letter phi (<b>ϕ</b>), covers values between 0 and π radians, or 0 to 180 degrees. Introducing Phi (<b>ϕ</b>) transitions us from polar coordinates to spherical coordinates",
               "source": [
